        <details class="qitem" open><summary>So what actually is it?</summary><p>A leaf from <b>Mitragyna speciosa</b>, a Southeast Asian tree in the coffee family. Brewed and chewed there for generations. The alkaloid people talk about is mitragynine, that&rsquo;s what we measure.</p></details>
        <details class="qitem"><summary>Will it get me high?</summary><p>It isn&rsquo;t THC and we won&rsquo;t pretend it&rsquo;s a substitute for anything. People describe steady energy or physical ease depending on the amount. Effects vary by person, and that&rsquo;s the honest answer.</p></details>
        <details class="qitem"><summary>Is it legal?</summary><p>In 32 states, yes. We don&rsquo;t ship to the other 18, <a href="{{ url_ship }}">here&rsquo;s the list</a>, and checkout blocks those addresses before you can pay.</p></details>
        <details class="qitem"><summary>How do I know what I&rsquo;m getting?</summary><p>Every batch is screened by an independent lab for identity, potency, heavy metals and microbials, and the batch number is printed on your pouch. <a href="{{ url_coa }}">Read the reports</a>.</p></details>
        <details class="qitem"><summary>Who shouldn&rsquo;t take it?</summary><p>Anyone under 21, anyone pregnant or nursing, and anyone on medication without talking to their clinician first. Regular daily use can build tolerance and habit, start low and take breaks.</p></details>
